at CES 2014 Sony showed off a prototype  virtual reality headset the h MZ t 3q  basically a motion tracker put on the  back of the existing head mounted  display they already have this new  version replicates the experience of  sitting in front of your own private 750  inch theater but the device can also  track your head movements allowing you  to look around and pan your view across  whatever virtual environment you're  exploring put on some headphones and you  can imagine that this is an immersive  relaxing way to pass some time on a long  plane ride watching some TV or a movie  but some people have made comparisons  between this device and the oculus rift  for the virtual reality headset from  oculus and if Sony's going after the  same audience their prototype device has  a long way to go but even more troubling  as the potential price again this was  just a prototype of no announced specs  or price points but it's based off  Sony's current headset which retails for  almost a thousand dollars and doesn't  include the motion tracking tech for  comparison oculus 2 now dev kits and  fear machines through Kickstarter for  $300 the Sony HMT headset may not be a  serious contender in this virtual  headset race yet but with a big name  company like the stepping into the arena  and shows that virtual reality is  something that start taking seriously
 

